Template Pack · doc-spine

Skeleton files for a new project. Copy them with the Quickstart block in the repo
README.md (mkdir + one cp per file, destinations included); HOWTO.md §4 is the
fill-in checklist that follows.

Note · the relative links inside these templates (e.g., `../STATE.md`, `docs/TASKS.md`, `../../docs/ROADMAP.md`) intentionally do NOT resolve from this `templates/` directory — they resolve once the file is in its target location in the new project.

Placeholders to fill in:
  <PROJECT_NAME>           project name
  <PROJECT_PATH>           memory directory path (e.g., -Users-yourname-work-myproject)
  <ACTIVE_INSTANCE>        active instance directory name
  <DOMAIN-SPECIFIC-RULE>   any domain-specific rule for your project
  <REGISTRY>               if you have a pure registry, e.g., HPC_inventory

Optional, none needed at bootstrap:
  - `.aiignore` in any frozen / read-only instance directory
  - a domain-specific entry in CONVENTIONS.md §6
  - research / writing projects: cp templates/lit-settle.reference.md → <PROJECT>/docs/
    (reference implementation of the literature settle step; see CONVENTIONS.md §10)
  - project closeout, if a human must retake ownership of the subject matter:
    cp templates/TUTORIAL_WRITING_STANDARD.md → <PROJECT>/docs/ (charter for the
    optional tutorial content type; see SPEC.md §3)
  - when a pivot-heavy phase begins: cp templates/INDEX.md → instances/<ACTIVE_INSTANCE>/scratch/INDEX.md
    (catalog for non-canonical exploration drafts; see SPEC §8.4)
